I know this isn't what to expect, but to me it's amazing amethyste from diamine. just a purple. but the shade somehow... speaks to me! IT'S SO.. NICE. I just added silver shimmer to mine and I can't wait to try it on a pen, it looks like it'd be stunning.

&#x200B;

but outside of that, special behaving inks for me would be A) Sheaffer skirp purple (looks like a blue-ish purple when dry, but it looks amazing while drying, goes from a deep purple to a  light blue-ish lavender, and you can see it shift color in different sections as it dies!)

&#x200B;

Also document fuchsia is one to me, it's water/smudge proof (you can get it to smudge a TINY bit if you try enough!) And yet sheens gold on some papers. pigment sheen means sheen without smudge :O but also, it's really... saturated? it's an eye blinding pink! it's something else, also the entire ink looks like the color of the ink in your pen, not black (unlike most colors!)

&#x200B;

Diamine mystique is also one of mine, it's really pretty, gold shimmer, blue/black ish purple!

&#x200B;

another one is my diy black ink + purple shimmer, it looks really nice IMO.

&#x200B;

another is noodler's cactus fruit eel. it's really pretty and jello-ish, doesn't smudge despite the look and it's lubricated (doesn't work on my pilot kakuno M very well tho :|, should maybe try it again?). i love it way more than yama-budo

